.\" Man page for corkscrew.
.TH CORKSCREW 1 "October 2026" "corkscrew 3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
corkscrew \- tunnel SSH through an HTTP proxy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B corkscrew
.RI [ options ]
.I proxyhost proxyport desthost destport
.RI [ authfile ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B corkscrew
connects to an HTTP proxy and asks it to establish a tunnel to
.I desthost:destport
with the HTTP CONNECT method.
The proxy response is parsed and the resulting byte stream is relayed
between standard input/output and the proxy connection.
It is commonly used as an OpenSSH
.B ProxyCommand
for reaching an SSH server through an HTTP proxy.
.PP
The proxy port and destination port are required decimal integers in the
range 1 through 65535.
IPv6 destination addresses may be supplied with or without brackets;
the CONNECT request uses the bracketed form.
.PP
Standard input and standard output must be open when
.B corkscrew
starts.
The proxy socket is always given a descriptor above the standard error
descriptor so that it cannot alias a closed standard stream.
.PP
The original positional form remains supported.
Options may be placed before, between, or after the positional arguments.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Report connection progress on standard error.
Credentials are never printed.
.TP
.BI \-\-connect\-timeout= seconds
Set the TCP connect deadline in seconds.
The default is 10 seconds.
.TP
.BI \-\-handshake\-timeout= seconds
Set the deadline for writing the CONNECT request and reading the proxy
response in seconds.
The default is 10 seconds.
.TP
.BI \-\-auth\-file= file
Read the proxy credential from
.I file
instead of the final positional argument.
The two forms cannot be combined.
.TP
.BI \-\-auth\-fd= fd
Read the proxy credential from an inherited descriptor.
The descriptor must be 3 or greater and is closed after one line is read.
This mode does not require a regular file and does not check file
permissions because descriptors may refer to pipes or other protected
streams supplied by a supervisor.
.TP
.B \-\-http11
Send an HTTP/1.1 CONNECT request with
.B Host
and
.B User-Agent
headers.
The default remains HTTP/1.0 for compatibility with older proxies.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
If
.I authfile
is given, the first line of the file is read as an HTTP Basic
authentication credential in the form
.RI username : password .
The line ending may be LF or CRLF.
Leading and trailing spaces are preserved, including trailing spaces before
the line ending.
.PP
The authentication file must be a regular file and must not be accessible
by group or other users.
Create it with a command such as:
.PP
.RS
.nf
umask 077
printf '%s\n' 'username:password' >~/.ssh/corkscrew-auth
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/corkscrew-auth
.fi
.RE
.PP
Credentials are encoded with Base64 for the
.B Proxy-Authorization
header.
Base64 is not encryption.
The proxy connection is plaintext HTTP unless an external transport
protects it.
.SH SIGNALS
During the relay,
.BR SIGTERM ,
.BR SIGINT ,
.BR SIGHUP ,
and
.B SIGQUIT
request an orderly shutdown.
Shared descriptor flags are restored before the process exits.
.B SIGTSTP
restores the inherited descriptor flags before stopping and reapplies
nonblocking mode after the process resumes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The tunnel reached end-of-file on both directions and closed normally.
.TP
.B 1
An argument, connection, authentication, handshake, or relay error
occurred.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was invalid and the usage message was printed.
.TP
.B 128+\fIsignal\fR
A termination signal was received during the relay.
.SH EXAMPLES
Use
.B corkscrew
directly:
.PP
.RS
.nf
corkscrew proxy.example.com 8080 ssh.example.com 22
.fi
.RE
.PP
Configure OpenSSH to use it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
Host ssh.example.com
    ProxyCommand /usr/local/bin/corkscrew proxy.example.com 8080 %h %p
.fi
.RE
.PP
With proxy authentication:
.PP
.RS
.nf
Host ssh.example.com
    ProxyCommand /usr/local/bin/corkscrew proxy.example.com 8080 %h %p ~/.ssh/corkscrew-auth
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use an integrated proxy header mode and explicit deadlines:
.PP
.RS
.nf
corkscrew --http11 --connect-timeout=5 --handshake-timeout=5 \\
    proxy.example.com 8080 ssh.example.com 22
.fi
.RE
.SH SECURITY
HTTP CONNECT carries the request and tunnel over a plaintext TCP
connection to the proxy.
Proxy Basic authentication is only Base64 encoded.
Use a trusted proxy or a protected network path, and do not reuse valuable
passwords.
.PP
The tunnel is not a substitute for SSH host-key verification.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh_config (5)
.SH AUTHORS
